<title>USA: Woolworth Q3 share rises to $0.52.</title>
<headline>Woolworth Q3 share rises to $0.52.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr     profit	   $0.52   profit	 $0.26</p>
<p> Net     profit	  69,000   profit	34,000</p>
<p> Sales		  2,048,000		2,071,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 133,600		  132,800</p>
<p>	   9 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr     profit	   $0.52     loss	 $0.43</p>
<p> Net     profit	  69,000     loss	57,000</p>
<p> Sales		  5,724,000		5,787,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 133,300		   132,800</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Full company name is Woolworth Corp</p>
<p>NOTE: The 3Q 1996 included costs related to disposed operations of $5 million, relecting the Silk &amp; Satin and Rubin transactions and the shutdown of Canadian distribution center. The first nine months include costs related to disposed operations of $36 million. In 3Q 1996, the company also reported a $18 million gain on sale of nonstrategic real estate and 1996 year to date included a $31 milion gain on such sales.</p>
